      "channelId": "UCAjsH3UCJrd-xAfUBsB-dOg",
      "title": "Technical Interview | Vertical Traversal of a Binary Tree",
      "description": "Coding interview. In this coding interview, I go over a vertical tree traversal question with a computer science university student.\n\nProblem:\nReturn the vertical traversal of a binary tree. The vertical traversal assigns a column depth to each node in the binary tree and then prints out the traversal going from the left-most column to the right-most column. Order within a specific column are determined by going from top to bottom in the binary tree.\n\nExample:\n\n     3 \n4       2       = [[4], [3, 2], [2], [5]]\n     2     5\n\nOne approach for solving this problem is to create a map which maps from level to the associated list for a column level and running BFS. BFS ensures we get a level by level traversal on the tree.\n\nThe solution approach taken in the video is to run DFS first and then sort the resulting map.",
